In the afternoon, I am sitting at my desk and looking at the laptop.
Sven comes over to me.
He is the tester on our team.
"Maya, I have tested the new feature," he says.
"Unfortunately, I have found a small bug."
"What exactly happened?" I ask.
Sven explains the problem to me very precisely.
"I clicked on the button," he says.
"But it didn't work."
I appreciate his sharp eye.
I have worked as a software engineer for many years.
But of course you sometimes make small mistakes.
I search for the problem in my program.
After a minute, I have already found the bug.
Only a short line of code is missing.
I type quickly and fix the feature.
"I have corrected the code," I say to Sven.
He tests the feature again on his computer.
"Great, now everything works!" he says happily.
We are truly already a solid team.
